  "details": "Make it possible to set avatar performance blocks based on every measured avatar performance stat.\n\nI frequently get tanked down to <5 fps because of avatars with thousands of physbone collision checks. I tune my download size and uncompressed size limits to try to indirectly filter these people out, but sometimes one will slip through. With tooling like Thry's VRAM optimizer becoming more well known, it's happening more often.\n\nI think that users should be able to performance block based on this attribute and anything else that is currently measured. You could put these less-often-used filters under an \"advanced\" dropdown in the \"Avatar Optimizations\" section of the big menu.",
